# Tokens for `basic_auth`. The input is
#   u8 work | u8 mutate | u8 hash | user \0 password \0 stored-hash \0 header
# so the NUL that ends a field is itself a token: without it the fuzzer
# spends its whole budget inside the user field and never reaches the
# header.
"\x00"

# --- the Authorization header -----------------------------------------
# The scheme is matched whole and case-insensitively; these are what tell
# an exact compare from a prefix or a case-folded one.
"Basic "
"basic "
"BASIC "
"Basicx "
"Bearer "
"bearer "
"Digest "
"Negotiate "
# Leading and interior whitespace: the value is trimmed on both sides.
# (libFuzzer's dictionary format knows only \\, \" and \xNN, so the tab is
# spelled \x09.)
" "
"\x09"
"  "

# --- base64, and the colon it hides -----------------------------------
":"
"="
"=="
"YWRhOmxvdmVsYWNl"
"Og=="
"OmE="
"YTo="
"YWRhOg=="
"OmxvdmVsYWNl"
# Valid base64 with no colon in it: decodes, but is not a credential.
"YWRh"
# Valid base64 of bytes that are not UTF-8.
"/w=="
"+/"

# --- stored hashes: the argon2 PHC grammar ----------------------------
"$"
"$argon2id$"
"$argon2i$"
"$argon2d$"
"v=19"
"v=16"
# Deliberately only the *minimum* parameter set. Measured: with
# `m=19456,t=2,p=1` in here the fuzzer assembles a default-cost hash out of
# these tokens within seconds and the target drops to ~13 exec/s, spending
# its whole budget inside the KDF rather than in the parsers this target is
# about. Nitr's own parameters are covered by the sampled round trip and by
# the `argon2-correct-password` seed; the cost ceilings are covered by the
# STORED table, which asserts them without running them.
"m=8,t=1,p=1"
"m=8,t=1,p=1$"
"mHVoGfzni7/d60QmEsVJlw"
"7rFvapCGZeh96Zf4R2I/pEVmV2YRWxfl6xo5yGL3F6Q"
"$argon2id$v=19$m=8,t=1,p=1$mHVoGfzni7/d60QmEsVJlw$7rFvapCGZeh96Zf4R2I/pEVmV2YRWxfl6xo5yGL3F6Q"
"keyid="
"data="

# --- stored hashes: everything that is not argon2 ---------------------
# The migration cases. None of these can verify, and each must say so.
"$2a$"
"$2b$12$"
"$2y$10$"
"$1$"
"$5$"
"$6$"
"$scrypt$"
"ln=16,r=8,p=1"
"$pbkdf2-sha256$"
"i=310000"
"{SSHA}"
"sha1$"
